138 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 96 0 R
/E (If this problem is ignored, intersections will remain dangerous. According to the Ministry of Road Transport and Highway, India sees over 1.6 lakh road accident fatalities annually, with jumping red lights and over-speeding being leading causes. Automated enforcement is proven to deter this reckless behavior, but it is only possible if the camera network is cheap enough to deploy everywhere. The World Bank estimates that road crashes cost the Indian economy approximately 3% of its GDP annually.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
139 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 96 0 R
/E (A highly scalable, low-cost network of edge cameras rapidly pays for itself by capturing thousands of automated challans that are currently being missed at unmonitored intersections, generating a steady revenue stream for city infrastructure.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
